### Pitsch backend — quick manual requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP client)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### Health (public): is the AI service reachable?
GET {{base}}/health

### Log in as the demo user (created on first start)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@pitsch.com", "password": "pitsch123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Submit a pitch email (attachments: base64, optional)
# @name email
POST {{base}}/emails/process
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sender": "ananya@krishiai.in",
  "senderName": "Ananya Rao",
  "subject": "Krishi AI - raising our $2M seed",
  "body": "Hi, I'm Ananya, CEO of Krishi AI. 12,000 farmers onboarded across 3 states; Rs 1.2 Cr ARR. Raising $2M seed.",
  "threadId": "thread-krishi-1"
}

###
@workflowId = {{email.response.body.workflowId}}

### Poll the workflow (status, availableActions, agents, brief, slots, draft)
GET {{base}}/workflows/{{workflowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Handle the pitch (runs Document -> Research -> Verification -> Analysis)
POST {{base}}/workflows/{{workflowId}}/action
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "COMPLETE_WORKFLOW" }

### Plan a meeting
POST {{base}}/workflows/{{workflowId}}/action
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "PLAN_MEETING" }

### Suggested slots
GET {{base}}/calendar/availability?workflowId={{workflowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Draft an email to the founder
POST {{base}}/workflows/{{workflowId}}/action
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "PLAN_EMAIL_RESPONSE" }

### Notifications
GET {{base}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
